# UI, ViewModel, data

Keep Android views out of ViewModels. UI observes data; ViewModels expose `LiveData` / `Flow` and call into a repository or data source.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — ViewModel holds a View and loads data itself
class SearchViewModel : ViewModel() {
    lateinit var recycler: RecyclerView
    fun search(q: String) = api.search(q)
}

// ✅ GOOD — immutable LiveData, query via switchMap, repository does I/O
class SearchViewModel(private val repo: RepoRepository) : ViewModel() {
    private val _query = MutableLiveData<String>()
    val results: LiveData<Resource<List<Repo>>> = _query.switchMap { q ->
        if (q.isBlank()) AbsentLiveData.create() else repo.search(q)
    }
    fun setQuery(input: String) { _query.value = input.trim() }
}
```

- Use `Transformations.switchMap` / `LiveData.switchMap` when one LiveData (query, id) should drive another.
- Use `SavedStateHandle` when the query must survive process death (`BasicSample`).
- Launch coroutines with `viewModelScope`; use `liveData { }` builders as in `LiveDataSample`.
- `GithubBrowserSample` wraps async results in `Resource` (`SUCCESS` / `ERROR` / `LOADING`) and loads via `NetworkBoundResource` (DB first, then network). Do not bypass that pattern in that sample.
